  "title": "Vrijeme i dani",
  "titleEn": "Weather and Days",
  "grammarTip": "To say 'on' a day of the week, Bosnian uses 'u' + the accusative case: u ponedjeljak, u utorak, u četvrtak and u petak look identical to the nominative (masculine nouns), but feminine day names change their ending: srijeda → u srijedu, subota → u subotu, nedjelja → u nedjelju. Weather is described with 'Vani je...' (It's... outside) followed by a fixed adverbial form that never changes: Vani je sunčano, vani je hladno, vani je toplo. Note that 'vrijeme' means both 'time' and 'weather' — context tells you which.",
